        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "eb737805-6b60-5dc4-bb96-3a87e4393d04",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alexander Trachtenberg, Joseph McCarthy\n- Laws: Smith Act\n- Events: McCarthyism, Second Red Scare\n- Organizations: U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals\n- Places: United States\n\nFacts:\n- The Second Red Scare in the United States lasted roughly from 1947 to 1956.\n- The term McCarthyism refers to U.S. Senator Joseph McCarthy.\n- McCarthyism was characterized by heightened political repression and a campaign spreading fear of influence on American institutions and of espionage by Soviet agents.\n- During McCarthyism in America, Alexander Trachtenberg was prosecuted twice and convicted under the Smith Act.\n- Alexander Trachtenberg’s first Smith Act conviction was overturned after a government witness recanted.\n- In 1958, the U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals overturned Alexander Trachtenberg’s second Smith Act conviction.",
